## 2. [`db.js`](file:///c:/Users/offic/OneDrive/Desktop/design%20thinking/db.js)

**Purpose:** Creates and exports a **MySQL connection pool** that all server routes share.

### How it works

```js
const pool = mysql.createPool({
  host: 'localhost',
  user: 'root',
  password: '****',        // Your MySQL root password
  database: 'library_db',  // Created by seed.js
  connectionLimit: 10,     // Max 10 simultaneous connections
});

module.exports = pool;
```

| Setting | Value | Why |
|---------|-------|-----|
| `waitForConnections` | `true` | Queues requests when all 10 connections are busy instead of throwing |
| `connectionLimit` | `10` | Prevents overwhelming MySQL with too many connections |
| `queueLimit` | `0` | Unlimited queue length (no request is rejected) |

> [!NOTE]
> This file is imported by `server.js`. Every API call uses `pool.query()` or `pool.getConnection()` from this pool.

