## 3. [`seed.js`](file:///c:/Users/offic/OneDrive/Desktop/design%20thinking/seed.js)

**Purpose:** One-time setup script. Run with `npm run seed` before first use.

### What it does (in order)

| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| 1 | Connects to MySQL **without** selecting a database |
| 2 | `CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS library_db` |
| 3 | Creates the `books` table |
| 4 | Creates the `transactions` table (with foreign key to `books`) |
| 5 | Clears any existing data & resets auto-increment |
| 6 | Inserts **20 books** with realistic rack locations |
| 7 | Inserts **4 sample transactions** (books that are pre-checked-out) |

### Database Schema

#### `books` table

| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `id` | `INT AUTO_INCREMENT` | Primary key |
| `title` | `VARCHAR(255)` | Book title |
| `author` | `VARCHAR(255)` | Author name |
| `isbn` | `VARCHAR(20)` | ISBN number |
| `rack_location` | `VARCHAR(100)` | Physical location, e.g. `"Floor 2, Row B, Rack 4"` |
| `is_available` | `TINYINT(1)` | `1` = on shelf, `0` = checked out |
| `created_at` | `TIMESTAMP` | Auto-set on insert |

#### `transactions` table

| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `id` | `INT AUTO_INCREMENT` | Primary key |
| `book_id` | `INT` | Foreign key → `books.id` (CASCADE on delete) |
| `student_id` | `VARCHAR(50)` | ID of student who borrowed the book |
| `issue_date` | `DATETIME` | When the book was issued (defaults to NOW) |
| `return_date` | `DATETIME NULL` | When returned (`NULL` = still checked out) |

