## 7. [`public/script.js`](file:///c:/Users/offic/OneDrive/Desktop/design%20thinking/public/script.js)

**Purpose:** All client-side logic — search, filtering, book cards rendering, issue/return workflows.

### Architecture

The script runs inside an **IIFE** (Immediately Invoked Function Expression) with `'use strict'` to avoid polluting the global scope.

### State Variables

| Variable | Type | Purpose |
|----------|------|---------|
| `allBooks` | `Array` | All books from the last API fetch |
| `activeFilter` | `String` | Current filter: `'all'`, `'available'`, or `'checked-out'` |
| `debounceTimer` | `Number` | Timer ID for debounced search |
| `issueBookId` | `Number` | Book ID currently being issued (set when modal opens) |

### Functions

#### Data Fetching

| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `fetchBooks(query)` | Calls `GET /api/books?search=...`, stores result in `allBooks`, then calls `renderBooks()` |

#### Rendering

| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `renderBooks()` | Filters `allBooks` by `activeFilter`, updates result count, generates card HTML, attaches button listeners |
| `cardHTML(book, index)` | Returns the HTML string for a single book card. Sets `--i` CSS variable for staggered animation |

#### Issue Flow

| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `openIssueModal(bookId, title)` | Opens the modal, focuses the Student ID input |
| `closeIssueModal()` | Hides the modal, resets `issueBookId` |
| `confirmIssue()` | Validates Student ID, calls `POST /api/books/issue`, shows toast, refreshes books |

#### Return Flow

| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `returnBook(bookId)` | Calls `POST /api/books/return`, shows toast, refreshes books |

#### Utilities

| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `toast(message, type)` | Creates a notification (`'success'`, `'error'`, or `'info'`). Auto-removes after 3.5 seconds |
| `showLoading(show)` | Toggles the loading spinner visibility |
| `esc(str)` | HTML-escapes a string to prevent XSS |

### Event Listeners

| Event | Element | Behavior |
|-------|---------|----------|
| `input` | Search input | Debounced (250ms) — calls `fetchBooks()` with current value |
| `click` | Clear button | Clears search, re-fetches all books |
| `click` | Filter pills | Sets `activeFilter`, re-renders without re-fetching |
| `click` | Issue button (on card) | Opens issue modal for that book |
| `click` | Return button (on card) | Immediately calls `returnBook()` |
| `click` | Modal overlay/close/cancel | Closes modal |
| `keydown` (Escape) | Document | Closes modal if open |
| `keydown` (Enter) | Student ID input | Confirms issue |

### Data Flow Diagram

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant script.js
    participant Express API
    participant MySQL

    User->>script.js: Types in search bar
    script.js->>script.js: Debounce 250ms
    script.js->>Express API: GET /api/books?search=...
    Express API->>MySQL: SELECT * FROM books WHERE ...
    MySQL-->>Express API: Rows
    Express API-->>script.js: JSON { books: [...] }
    script.js->>script.js: renderBooks() → inject card HTML

    User->>script.js: Clicks "Issue Book"
    script.js->>script.js: Open modal, prompt for Student ID
    User->>script.js: Enters ID, clicks Confirm
    script.js->>Express API: POST /api/books/issue { bookId, studentId }
    Express API->>MySQL: BEGIN → FOR UPDATE → UPDATE → INSERT → COMMIT
    MySQL-->>Express API: Success
    Express API-->>script.js: { success: true, message: "..." }
    script.js->>script.js: Toast notification + refresh grid

    User->>script.js: Clicks "Return Book"
    script.js->>Express API: POST /api/books/return { bookId }
    Express API->>MySQL: BEGIN → FOR UPDATE → UPDATE → UPDATE → COMMIT
    MySQL-->>Express API: Success
    Express API-->>script.js: { success: true, message: "..." }
    script.js->>script.js: Toast notification + refresh grid
```

